   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What someone else said",
     "texto": [
      "After **dire** the word **che** is used to introduce what was said: **Dice che arriva domani** (he says he's arriving tomorrow).",
      "**Mi ha detto che è stanco** means he is still tired now; **Mi ha detto che era stanco** presents the tiredness as past. The tense depends on when the situation happens."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Giving an opinion without changing register",
     "texto": [
      "To express an opinion with the indicative you can say **Secondo me, è giusto** (in my opinion, it's right).",
      "**Penso/credo che** usually takes the subjunctive in careful Italian (**penso che sia**); the indicative appears in familiar speech. It is recognised here, but we practise the simple form **secondo me + indicative**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
